Candidate fix for upstream llama.cpp, prepared against ggml-org/llama.cpp b23efaa2ef147f547ee75cbf0c621d61904de80e (2026-09-20).
NOT SUBMITTED. llama.cpp accepts contributions only from a human who understands and describes them; see docs/upstream-candidates.md.

Problem: with an F16 KV cache the CPU flash-attention decode path accumulates V in FP16 (VKQ16 / ggml_vec_mad_f16). Reproduce with
tools/fa_mqa_check.cpp linked against a stock upstream ggml build: relative RMS error against float64 is 6.4e-3 for 3 queries over
2,051 visible cells and 1.6e-3 to 2.0e-3 for one query; the tiled prefill path (F32 accumulators) is not affected.

This minimal change accumulates in F32 and converts each V row with ggml_cpu_fp16_to_fp32 (the SIMD converter). The generic
to_float trait is a scalar table walk and made the op 7x slower, so it is not used.

Measured on the upstream build, 15 workers, AVX-512, same program:
                                   stock            this patch
  2,051 of 4,096 visible, 3 q      6.39e-3  1.12 ms     8.55e-5  1.31 ms
  2,051 of 4,096 visible, 1 q      1.56e-3  0.32 ms     8.44e-5  0.38 ms
  2,051 of 32,768 visible, 3 q     6.67e-3  1.65 ms     8.93e-5  1.95 ms
  4,000 of 4,096 visible, 1 q      2.03e-3  0.49 ms     1.06e-4  0.59 ms
So: 75x more accurate for +17-21% time in this op. The remaining 8.5e-5 comes from the F16 Q.K dot product, left alone here.
A fused "mad from f16 into an f32 accumulator" helper should recover the time; that is not written. Only x86 was measured.

